WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:05.760
Speaker 1: The dangerous and unhinged CPAC
speech wasn't Trump's only public declaration

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.760
at CPAC in Washington, D.C. over the weekend.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:15.030
He also gave a very strange press conference
during which he came out looking extraordinarily

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.650
pale, disheveled and even visibly confused.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:21.670
He took a few questions, and there are just
a few moments here that I want to highlight

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:22.760
for you.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:26.070
One of the topics that we've been talking
about recently is this loyalty pledge.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:30.769
The Republican National Committee wants all
of the Republican candidates to sign a loyalty

00:00:30.769 --> 00:00:36.050
pledge wherein they will say in exchange for
being allowed on the debate stage.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:39.410
I will eventually support whoever is the Republican
nominee.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:41.090
Now, we've been going back and forth.

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:44.780
Is that something that Trump would be willing
to agree to or not?

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:47.750
One side is no, of course he's not going to
agree to it.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:51.340
The other side is sure he'll agree to it if
he needs to in order to get on the stage,

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:52.910
but then he won't abide by it.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:57.340
Well, Trump was actually asked about the loyalty
pledge, and at least for now, he seems to

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:58.960
be saying, I don't know.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.760
There's some people running that I wouldn't
be big on supporting.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.430
So unclear whether that loyalty pledge is
something he's going to go for.

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:06.430
Let's take a listen.

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:07.430
Speaker 2: I'm happy about it.

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:09.690
Speaker 1: A lot of the people we talked to,
the.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:16.020
Speaker 3: RNC who said they might have to
sign a loyalty pledge to participate in their

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:17.020
debates.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:18.020
That's something you would do or.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:19.020
Speaker 2: I don't know.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:20.549
I mean, I'm just hearing about it for the
first time, about the loyalty last year, probably

00:01:20.549 --> 00:01:24.710
people that I wouldn't be very happy about
endorsing in running.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:25.770
So we'll see.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:27.700
I think some of them I won't use names.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:31.960
I don't want to insult anybody, but some of
them I would not be very happy about.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:33.370
So I'll have to think about that.

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:34.370
Speaker 1: Yeah.

00:01:34.370 --> 00:01:37.930
So Trump saying fundamentally, and this is
an honest answer, right?

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:42.509
There are people running or potentially running
or likely running that he wouldn't actually

00:01:42.509 --> 00:01:43.530
want to support.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:44.950
So he's going to have to think about it now.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:50.000
I still think that the truth is, when push
comes to shove, Trump, if he absolutely needs

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.670
to get on the debate stage, he will sign whatever
he will say, whatever he wants to be on the

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:55.670
debate stage.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:59.250
And if that's going to prevent him, if not,
signing the loyalty pledge will keep him off

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:00.250
the debate stage.

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:01.399
He'll just sign it.

00:02:01.399 --> 00:02:06.729
And then if it comes down to he loses the
nomination and then he wants to run as an

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:08.879
independent, he'll just ignore it all.

00:02:08.879 --> 00:02:12.489
He'll say, you know, when I signed it, I didn't
assume they would rig it against me or whatever.

00:02:12.489 --> 00:02:14.640
I still think that that is the most likely
thing.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:18.879
These pledges, promises, they mean absolutely
nothing to Donald Trump.

00:02:18.879 --> 00:02:23.569
At another moment, Donald Trump was asked
about some of the things that Mike Pompeo,

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:28.170
his own former secretary, one of his own former
secretaries of state, said during Pompeo's

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:29.750
own CPAC speech.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:34.850
And Pompeo said, we don't need celebrity nominees.

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:38.220
And Trump was asked, Do you think Pompeo was
talking about you?

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:42.379
And Trump basically said, I don't see myself
as a celebrity, so probably not.

00:02:42.379 --> 00:02:51.430
Speaker 2: Mike Pompeo Yesterday, we talked
about how the regime follows the networks

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:52.769
of leaders based on fragile egos and refused
to acknowledge reality.

00:02:52.769 --> 00:02:53.769
Was he talking about the other ones?

00:02:53.769 --> 00:02:54.769
No, I don't think he was talking about me.

00:02:54.769 --> 00:02:55.950
I don't consider myself a celebrity leader.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:59.270
I consider myself the leader of the country.

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:00.970
I don't consider myself a celebrity leader.

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:02.080
Speaker 1: How insane is.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:05.280
Speaker 2: This into this film celebrity?

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.590
Maybe it helped me get elected.

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:07.590
Who knows?

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:08.590
But I don't consider that.

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:12.170
I consider myself a person that was president
for four years.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:13.220
Speaker 1: Yeah.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:15.440
Trump doesn't consider himself a celebrity,
of course.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:19.660
The reality is, were Trump not a celebrity
celebrity, he never would have become the

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.530
Republican nominee to begin with.

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:24.730
But okay, he can live in whatever fantasy
world he wants to live in.

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:30.600
And then lastly, the topic came up during
this press conference Trump gave.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:35.299
Of if you are indicted, will you still run
for president?

00:03:35.299 --> 00:03:37.070
And Trump said he would.

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:39.200
Here's like a little report on this from ABC.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:44.730
Speaker 4: Trump himself faces multiple state
and federal criminal investigations and lawsuits,

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:49.440
but he told reporters none of them will force
him out of the race, even if he is indicted.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.170
Speaker 2: So you'll stay in the race?

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:52.170
Oh, absolutely, I will.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:53.330
Do you even think about leaving?

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:58.670
Speaker 4: While Trump dominated CPAC, Florida
Governor Ron DeSantis spoke this weekend at

00:03:58.670 --> 00:03:59.670
the Reagan Library.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:00.670
Speaker 1: Okay.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:03.989
So Trump saying he would absolutely stay in
if he is indicted.

00:04:03.989 --> 00:04:06.599
Now, I think that that statement is meaningless.

00:04:06.599 --> 00:04:12.920
And what I mean by that is Trump has no choice
but to say he would stay in because if he

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:16.720
says, oh, no, no, no, if I'm indicted, I'm
leaving.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:21.910
He immediately short circuits donations, he
short circuit support because there will be

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:24.220
people who will hear that and say, oh, wait
a second.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:26.600
My going to support this guy or donate to
this guy.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:29.630
If he bails, if he's indicted.

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:30.630
No.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:33.229
So regardless of what the truth is, Trump
has to say he would stay in.

00:04:33.229 --> 00:04:39.220
In reality, in practice, if Trump is indicted,
depending on what the charges are, depending

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:43.310
on what's going on, I think it will potentially
affect his race.

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:49.720
Now, whether he actually bails or whether
it just destroys his chances of winning are

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:53.880
two different scenarios which we can discuss
at some future point.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:58.500
But I think Trump has no choice but to say
exactly this at this point in time, and we'll

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:00.460
see what the truth is if and when it happens.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:04.490
And by the way, reports are that the indictment
may come down any time.

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:07.630
As I like to say, it could come down today
or never.

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:08.630
That's the range.

00:05:08.630 --> 00:06:29.249
Anytime between today and never, Trump could
be indicted.

